      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We present the case of a 49 year old woman who was admitted to the emergency department for dyspnoea, transient amaurosis and limbs oedema. During hospitalisation a full workup revealed multisystemic thrombosis and dilated cardiomyopathy in relation with viral myocarditis due to Coxackie B infection. Diagnosis and treatment will be discussed in light of the litterature."},
